  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.Thirumoorthy vs The Food Safety Officer on 20 March, 2024 Author: T.V.Thamilselvi Bench: T.V.Thamilselvi 1 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 20.03.2024 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mrs.Justice T.V.Thamilselvi Crl.Op No. 5969 of 2022 & Crl.MP. Nos. 3318 & 3321 of 2022 P.Thirumoorthy Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Coimbatore Corporation Section, Code No. 563. 219, Race Course Road, Coimbatore - 641 018. ...Responde Prayer : This petition has been filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C , call for records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C.No.5175 of 2020 file of the Honble Judicial Magistrate Court No.V Coimbatore and gr such other further relieves as this Honble High Court deems fit and necessary in the nature and circumstances of the case and thus rend For Petitioner : Mr.M.Rajaraman For Respondent : Mr.s.Vinoth Kumar Government Advocate (C ORDER T h e p e t i t i o n e r h e r e i n f i l e d t h i s p e t i t i o n t o c a l l f o r r e c o r d s a n d q u a s h https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis the proceedings in S.T.C.No.5175 of 2020 on the file of the Honble Judicial Magistrate Court No.V Coimbatore. P.Thirumoorthy vs The Food Safety Officer on 20 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/83061876/ 1 2.",
    "facts": "The complainant had sought for permission to file a case against the accused to the designated officer and the same was granted by the commissioner of Food Safety and hence he has filed the above complaint before the Judicial https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Magistrate No. V Coimbatore under the provisions of Section 59 (i) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and 190(1)(A) and 200 C.P.C. Hence, the petitioner filed this petition to quash the proceedings in S.T.C No. 5175 of 2020 pending on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No. V, Coimbatore. Therefore, the petitioner was not able send the food sample to referral laboratory owing to the delay on the part of the complainant/respondent.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioner submits that as per Section 42 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, Food analyst ought to have analysed the sample and send the analysis report within 14 days to the designated officer but in the present case sample had taken on 28.06.2019 and the Food analyst had analysed the sample from 01.07.2019 to 31.01.2020 and thereafter issued report on 31.01.2020 which is contrary to the above Section which had deprived the petitioner's valuable to appeal as contemplated under Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006."
  },
